            <ArticleTitle>The pain of nasal tampon removal after nasal surgery: a randomized control trial.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>215-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.otohns.2008.09.012</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">The purpose of this study was to compare the pain and discomfort associated with the removal of two commercially available nasal tampons after nasal surgery.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="STUDY DESIGN" NlmCategory="METHODS">Prospective, paired, randomized clinical trial.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="SUBJECTS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Consecutive, consenting, adult patients undergoing nasal surgery.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="INTERVENTIONS" NlmCategory="METHODS">The nose was packed with a Rapid Rhino tampon (Applied Therapeutics, Tampa, FL) on one side and a Rhino Rocket tampon (Shippert Medical Technologies Corporation, Centennial, CO) on the other.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="OUTCOMES" NlmCategory="RESULTS">The pain of packing removal was assessed with a validated 100-mm visual analog scale. Patient satisfaction was measured on a Likert scale from 1 to 5.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">In all 13 patients, the pain of removal was greater with the Rhino Rocket Tampon (82.7 +/- 20.9 mm) than with the Rapid Rhino tampon (12.0 +/- 11.9 mm); the mean difference was 70.7 mm (95% confidence interval [CI], 47.1-78.2 mm; P &lt; 0.0001). Patient satisfaction was significantly higher with the Rapid Rhino nasal tampon (4.6 +/- 1.1 vs 1.5 +/- 0.7; mean difference 3.1 [95% CI, 2.6-3.6]; P &lt; 0.001).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Removal of the Rapid Rhino nasal tampon was significantly less painful and was associated with higher patient satisfaction than the removal of the Rhino Rocket nasal tampon.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
